ot/sotopia/-/value_stream_analytics)\\n    * [ Contributor analytics  ](/root/sotopia/-/graphs/main?ref_type=heads)\\n    * [ CI/CD analytics  ](/root/sotopia/-/pipelines/charts)\\n    * [ Repository analytics  ](/root/sotopia/-/graphs/main/charts)\\n    * [ Model experiments  ](/root/sotopia/-/ml/experiments)\\n\\n  * * * *\\n\\nSettings \\n\\n    * [ General  ](/root/sotopia/edit)\\n    * [ Integrations  ](/root/sotopia/-/settings/integrations)\\n    * [ Webhooks  ](/root/sotopia/-/hooks)\\n    * [ Access tokens  ](/root/sotopia/-/settings/access_tokens)\\n    * [ Repository  ](/root/sotopia/-/settings/repository)\\n    * [ Merge requests  ](/root/sotopia/-/settings/merge_requests)\\n    * [ CI/CD  ](/root/sotopia/-/settings/ci_cd)\\n    * [ Packages and registries  ](/root/sotopia/-/settings/packages_and_registries)\\n    * [ Monitor  ](/root/sotopia/-/settings/operations)\\n    * [ Usage Quotas  ](/root/sotopia/-/usage_quotas)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nHelp \\n\\n  *     * [ Help  ](/help)\\n    * [ Support  ](https://about.gitlab.com/get-help/)\\n    * [ GitLab documentation  ](/help/docs)\\n    * [ Compare GitLab plans  ](https://about.gitlab.com/pricing)\\n    * [ Community forum  ](https://forum.gitlab.com)\\n    * [ Contribute to GitLab  ](/help#contribute-to-gitlab)\\n    * [ Provide feedback  ](https://about.gitlab.com/submit-feedback)\\n  *     * Keyboard shortcuts ` ? `\\n    * What's new  4 \\n\\n\\n\\n[ Admin  ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin)\\n\\n[ Milestones ](/dashboard/milestones) [ Snippets ](/dashboard/snippets) [ Activity ](/dashboard/activity) [ Groups ](/dashboard/groups) [ Projects ](/dashboard/projects) [ Create a new issue ](/root/sotopia/-/issues/new)\\n\\n<::before>\\n\\nTo help improve GitLab, we would like to periodically [ collect usage information ](/help/administration/settings/usage_statistics.md) . This can be changed at any time in [ your settings ](/admin/application_settings/metrics_and_profiling#js-usage-settings) . \\n\\n[ Send service data  ](/admin/application_settings?application_setting%5Busage_ping_enabled%5D=1&application_setting%5Bversion_check_enabled%5D=1) [ Don't send service data  ](/admin/application_settings?application_setting%5Busage_ping_enabled%5D=0&application_setting%5Bversion_check_enabled%5D=0)\\n\\n  1. <::after> [ Administrator  ](/root)\\n  2. <::after> [ sotopia  ](/root/sotopia)\\n  3. [ General Settings  ](/root/sotopia/edit)\\n\\n\\n\\n#  General Settings \\n\\nCollapse \\n\\n##  Naming, description, topics \\n\\nUpdate your project name, description, avatar, and topics. [ Learn more about projects ](/help/user/project/working_with_projects.md) . \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nProject name  Must start with letter, digit, emoji, or underscore. Can also contain periods, dashes, spaces, and parentheses. \\n\\nProject ID \\n\\nS \\n\\nProject avatar  Choose file\u2026  No file chosen. \\n\\nThe ideal image size is 192 x 192 pixels. The maximum file size allowed is 200 KiB. \\n\\nThe maximum file size is 200 KiB. \\n\\nProject description (optional)  Sotopia: an Open-ended Social Learning Environment (ICLR 2024 spotlight)\\n\\nRepository size limit (MiB) \\n\\nWant to use this feature for free?  Read more about the [ Registration Features Program ](/help/administration/settings/usage_statistics.md#registration-features-program) . \\n\\nProject topics \\n\\n  * No matches found \\n\\n\\n\\n\\nTopics are publicly visible even on private projects. Do not include sensitive information in topic names. [ Learn more ](/help/user/project/project_topics) . \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Visibility, project features, permissions \\n\\nChoose visibility level, enable/disable project features and their permissions, disable email notifications, and show default emoji reactions. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nProject visibility \\n\\nManage who can see the project in the public access directory.  [ Learn more ](/help/user/public_access.md) . \\n\\nPrivate  Internal  Public \\n\\nAccessible by anyone, regardless of authentication. \\n\\n**Additional options** Users can request access \\n\\nIssues \\n\\nFlexible tool to collaboratively develop ideas and plan work in this project.  [ Learn more ](/help/user/project/issues/index.md) . \\n\\nIssues \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nRepository \\n\\nView and edit files in this project. When set to **Everyone With Access** non-project members have only read access. \\n\\nRepository \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nMerge requests \\n\\nSubmit changes to be merged upstream. \\n\\nMerge requests \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nForks \\n\\nUsers can copy the repository to a new project. \\n\\nForks \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nGit Large File Storage (LFS) \\n\\nManages large files such as audio, video, and graphics files.  [ Learn more ](/help/topics/git/lfs/index.md) . \\n\\nGit Large File Storage (LFS) \\n\\nCI/CD \\n\\nBuild, test, and deploy your changes. Does not apply to project integrations. \\n\\nCI/CD \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nAnalytics \\n\\nView project analytics. \\n\\nAnalytics \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nSecurity and compliance \\n\\nSecurity and compliance for this project. \\n\\nSecurity and compliance \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nWiki \\n\\nPages for project documentation. \\n\\nWiki \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nSnippets \\n\\nShare code with others outside the project. \\n\\nSnippets \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nPackage registry \\n\\nPublish, store, and view packages in a project.  [ Learn more ](/help/user/packages/index.md) . \\n\\nPackage registry \\n\\nModel experiments \\n\\nTrack machine learning model experiments and artifacts.  [ Learn more ](/help/user/project/ml/experiment_tracking/index.md) . \\n\\nModel experiments \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nModel registry \\n\\nManage machine learning models.  [ Learn more ](/help/user/project/ml/model_registry/index.md) . \\n\\nModel registry \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nMonitor \\n\\nMonitor the health of your project and respond to incidents. \\n\\nMonitor \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nEnvironments \\n\\nEvery project can make deployments to environments either via CI/CD or API calls. Non-project members have read-only access.  [ Learn more ](/help/ci/environments/index.md) . \\n\\nEnvironments \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nFeature flags \\n\\nRoll out new features without redeploying with feature flags.  [ Learn more ](/help/operations/feature_flags.md) . \\n\\nFeature flags \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nInfrastructure \\n\\nConfigure your infrastructure.  [ Learn more ](/help/user/infrastructure/index.md) . \\n\\nInfrastructure \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\nReleases \\n\\nCombine git tags with release notes, release evidence, and assets to create a release.  [ Learn more ](/help/user/project/releases/index.md) . \\n\\nReleases \\n\\nOnly Project Members  Everyone With Access \\n\\n#####  Email notifications \\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable email notifications \\n\\nEnable sending email notifications for this project \\n\\n<::before><::after> Include diff previews \\n\\nEmails are not encrypted. Concerned administrators may want to disable diff previews. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Show default emoji reactions \\n\\nAlways show thumbs-up and thumbs-down emoji buttons on issues, merge requests, and snippets. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Warn about Potentially Unwanted Characters \\n\\nHighlight the usage of hidden unicode characters. These have innocent uses for right-to-left languages, but can also be used in potential exploits. \\n\\nCI/CD Catalog project \\n\\nSet component project as a CI/CD Catalog project. [ What is the CI/CD Catalog? ](/help/ci/components/index#cicd-catalog)\\n\\nCI/CD Catalog project \\n\\nThe project will be findable in the CI/CD Catalog after the project has at least one release. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Badges \\n\\nAdd badges to display information about this project. [ What are badges? ](/help/user/project/badges.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Your badges  0 \\n\\nAdd new badge \\n\\nName  |  Badge  |  URL  |  Actions   \\n---|---|---|---  \\nThis project has no badges. Start by adding a new badge.   \\n  \\nExpand \\n\\n##  Service Desk \\n\\nEnable and disable Service Desk. Some additional configuration might be required. [ Learn more ](/help/user/project/service_desk/index.md) . \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Improve customer support with Service Desk \\n\\nService Desk allows people to create issues in your GitLab instance without their own user account. It provides a unique email address for end users to create issues in a project. Replies can be sent either through the GitLab interface or by email. End users only see threads through email. \\n\\n[ Configure Service Desk  ](/help/user/project/service_desk/configure.md)\\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Advanced \\n\\nHousekeeping, export, archive, change path, transfer, and delete. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n####  Housekeeping \\n\\nRuns a number of housekeeping tasks within the current repository, such as compressing file revisions and removing unreachable objects. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/housekeeping.md)\\n\\n[ Run housekeeping  ](/root/sotopia/housekeeping) Prune unreachable objects \\n\\n####  Export project \\n\\nExport this project with all its related data in order to move it to a new GitLab instance. When the exported file is ready, you can download it from this page or from the download link in the email notification you will receive. You can then import it when creating a new project. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/settings/import_export.md)\\n\\nThe following items will be exported: \\n\\n  * <::marker>Project and wiki repositories \\n  * <::marker>Project uploads \\n  * <::marker>Project configuration, excluding integrations \\n  * <::marker>Issues with comments, merge requests with diffs and comments, labels, milestones, snippets, and other project entities \\n  * <::marker>LFS objects \\n  * <::marker>Issue Boards \\n  * <::marker>Design Management files and data \\n\\n\\n\\nThe following items will NOT be exported: \\n\\n  * <::marker>Job logs and artifacts \\n  * <::marker>Container registry images \\n  * <::marker>CI variables \\n  * <::marker>Pipeline triggers \\n  * <::marker>Webhooks \\n  * <::marker>Any encrypted tokens \\n\\n\\n\\n[ Export project  ](/root/sotopia/export)\\n\\n####  Archive project \\n\\nArchiving the project makes it entirely read-only. It is hidden from the dashboard and doesn't display in searches. **The repository cannot be committed to, and no issues, comments, or other entities can be created.** [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/working_with_projects.md#archive-a-project)\\n\\n[ Archive project  ](/root/sotopia/archive)\\n\\n####  Change path \\n\\nA project\u2019s repository name defines its URL (the one you use to access the project via a browser) and its place on the file disk where GitLab is installed. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/working_with_projects.md#rename-a-repository)\\n\\n  * <::marker>Be careful. Renaming a project's repository can have unintended side effects. \\n  * <::marker>You will need to update your local repositories to point to the new location. \\n\\nPath \\n\\nhttp://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/ \\n\\nChange path \\n\\n####  Transfer project \\n\\nTransfer your project into another namespace. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/settings/migrate_projects.md#transfer-a-project-to-another-namespace)\\n\\nA project\u2019s repository name defines its URL (the one you use to access the project via a browser) and its place on the file disk where